meta {
  name: List Products
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products?_fields=sku&_fields=status
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Accept: application/json
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.data: isArray
  res.body.pagination: isDefined
}

docs {
  `GET /api/v3/products` — search, filter, and page through products. All query
  parameters (`_fields`, `_page`, `_page_size`, `_sort_by`, filter params) are
  undeclared in `openapi_pimv3.json` but confirmed working live (2026-09-04/07
  against "David's Dev Account"). See `config/api-testing.config.md` quirks #7-13.

  ## This resolves the v3-unreachable blocker
  v3 is live and matches its documented shape. It was unreachable earlier only
  because it was tested against the wrong host/account (`pim.plytix.com` under the
  "API Docs" account) — v3 for this engagement is served from a separate DEV
  host/account. See `config/api-testing.config.md` for the full history.

  ## Spec discrepancy — missing query parameters
  `openapi_pimv3.json`'s `GET /api/v3/products` declares **zero** query params.
  All of the following work live and must be flagged to Plytix:
  - `_fields=<field>` (repeatable): sparse field selection.
  - `_page` + `_page_size`: page-number pagination. Default page size is 25.
  - `_sort_by=<field>`: ascending sort.
  - `<field>=<value>`: plain field equality filter (e.g. `sku=BAG-10157`).
  - `<field>[<op>]=<value>`: operator filter (e.g. `created[gt]=2026-01-01`).
  - `<related>.<field>=<value>`: related-entity dot filter (e.g. `categories.name=Backpacks`).
  - `attributes.<name>=<value>` / `attributes.<name>[<op>]=<value>`: custom attribute filters.

  ## `_fields` / `_expand` edge cases
  - `_fields=category_ids` **400s** (`HiddenFieldError: Field 'category_ids' does not
    exist in model 'Product'`). Use `_fields=categories` — returns fully expanded
    category objects.
  - `_fields=relationships` is **silently dropped** (200, field absent). The real
    field is `product_relationships`.
  - `_expand=<relationship>` **400s** (`InvalidFieldError`). Expansion is automatic
    per `_fields` value — no `_expand` needed.

  ## Pagination (confirmed 2026-09-07)
  - Default page size: 25. `pagination.next_page` is always a full URL (cursor style).
  - `_page` + `_page_size`: works (see Pagination example below).
  - `_offset` + `_limit`: **400** `InvalidFieldError` — not supported on this resource.

  ## Filter dialect
  `API V3.md` lists a JSON-object "Current" syntax and a query-string "Possible
  Alternative". v3 implements the **query-string** dialect. Confirmed live: plain
  field (`sku=BAG-10157`), operator (`created[gt]=2026-01-01`), related-entity dot
  (`categories.name=Backpacks`), custom attribute (`attributes.brand[icontains]=Plytix`).

  See examples below for representative responses for each scenario.
}

example {
  name: Sparse Field Selection
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-04. Two _fields params return only sku and status per product; pagination.next_page carries the cursor forward.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products?_fields=sku&_fields=status
    method: get
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [
            {
              "id": "6a38f614c3d65a5f868b1a06",
              "sku": "BAG-10157",
              "status": "Completed"
            },
            {
              "id": "6aa022262b6fd055ffb7caa4",
              "sku": "WC-TEST-FULL-001",
              "status": null
            }
          ],
          "errors": [],
          "pagination": {
            "next_page": "https://pim.dev.plytix.com/api/v3/products?_fields=sku&_fields=status&_page=2"
          }
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: Pagination - _page / _page_size
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-07. _page_size=2 returns exactly 2 items; pagination.next_page contains _page=2 and preserves all other query params. Note: _offset/_limit returns 400 InvalidFieldError and is not supported.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products?_fields=id&_fields=sku&_page=1&_page_size=2
    method: get
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [
            {
              "id": "6a38f614c3d65a5f868b1a06",
              "sku": "BAG-10157"
            },
            {
              "id": "6a38f614c3d65a5f868b1a07",
              "sku": "BAG-10158"
            }
          ],
          "errors": [],
          "pagination": {
            "next_page": "https://pim.dev.plytix.com/api/v3/products?_fields=id&_fields=sku&_page=2&_page_size=2"
          }
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: Plain Field Filter - sku
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-07. sku=BAG-10157 returns exactly one matching product; pagination.next_page is null when the result set is exhausted. Operator (created[gt]=...) and related-entity dot (categories.name=Backpacks) filters also confirmed working in the same query-string dialect.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products?_fields=id&_fields=sku&sku=BAG-10157
    method: get
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [
            {
              "id": "6a38f614c3d65a5f868b1a06",
              "sku": "BAG-10157"
            }
          ],
          "errors": [],
          "pagination": {
            "next_page": null
          }
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}
